1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,049
With two sets of bars, write about the gaps, not the heights.

2
00:00:04,049 --> 00:00:09,427
Here, village and city household spending, in thousands of rupees a month.

3
00:00:09,427 --> 00:00:15,481
The city spends more on every heading, about forty eight thousand against twenty thousand in total.

4
00:00:15,481 --> 00:00:27,330
Food is the biggest item for both, but it is nearly half of the village budget and under a third of the city's: turning bars into a share of the whole is the comparison grade twelve wants.

5
00:00:27,330 --> 00:00:31,002
The widest gap is housing: six times as much.

6
00:00:31,002 --> 00:00:32,890
The narrowest is health.

